cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "agda-deans-problem: the formal development of a paper on Dean's problem"
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  The formal development, in Agda, of the paper "No free lattice contains an
  infinite ascending chain of copies of FL(3)" by William DeMeo and Ralph
  Freese, which answers R. A. Dean's question in the negative: no free
  lattice contains an infinite strictly ascending chain of sublattices, each
  isomorphic to the free lattice on three generators.  The main theorem is
  proved for free lattices over generators with decidable equality, by finite
  searches and induction; the paper says which of its other statements are
  checked, and in what form.  It builds on the lattice library agda-lattices, pinned at one
  commit, and the Agda Universal Algebra Library.  Every module is checked
  under --without-K --exact-split --safe.
authors:
  - family-names: "DeMeo"
    given-names: "William"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1832-5690"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ualib/agda-deans-problem"
keywords:
  - Agda
  - lattice theory
  - free lattices
  - Dean's problem
  - formal verification
